From: OpenHarmony PC porting (libomptarget-rtl-amdgpu 18.1.8)
Subject: [PATCH] openmp/cmake: let an explicit ENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS override win

OpenMPTesting.cmake unconditionally sets ENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS back to TRUE
on every include, so `-DENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS=OFF` (documented way to build
without the lit test suites, e.g. when clang is not built in-tree) has no
effect and configure fails on add_dependencies(clang) for check-* targets.

Respect an explicit definition instead of silently discarding it.  Behavior
unchanged for all default builds.

--- a/openmp/cmake/OpenMPTesting.cmake
+++ b/openmp/cmake/OpenMPTesting.cmake
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Keep track if we have all dependencies.
-set(ENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS TRUE)
+if(NOT DEFINED ENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS)
+  set(ENABLE_CHECK_TARGETS TRUE)
+endif()
 
 # Function to find required dependencies for testing.
 function(find_standalone_test_dependencies)
